      <div class="two-column angle-layout">
        <div>
          <p>
            The total station was set up at survey stations and used to observe horizontal
            directions to target points. Direct and reverse observations were recorded so the
            readings could be checked and averaged.
          </p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li>Tripod setup and instrument security</li>
            <li>Centering and leveling</li>
            <li>Target sighting and focusing</li>
            <li>Direct and reverse observations</li>
            <li>Comparison of repeated readings</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <figure class="image-card angle-card">
          <img src="assets/angle-measurement-clean.svg" alt="Clean editable diagram showing three total-station sight lines from P to Q, R and S">
          <figcaption>Clean redraw of the three sight lines used for the angle-measurement exercise.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- =========================================
         TRIGONOMETRIC LEVELING
         ========================================= -->
    <section class="section dark" id="trig">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">05 · TRIGONOMETRIC LEVELING</p>
        <h2>Using geometry to determine elevation.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="two-column">
        <div>
          <p>
            Trigonometric leveling used the total station to combine measured distance, zenith
            angle, instrument height, and target height. The vertical component was determined
            from the observed slope distance and angle.
          </p>
          <div class="formula light large">V = S cos(Z) = S sin(α)</div>
          <div class="formula light large">ΔElev = hᵢ + V − hᵣ</div>
          <div class="metric-row">
            <div><strong>97.0032 m</strong><span>Observed benchmark elevation</span></div>
            <div><strong>0.0032 m</strong><span>Benchmark misclosure</span></div>
            <div><strong>0.0073615 m</strong><span>Permissible closure</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figure class="diagram-card">
          <img src="assets/trig-leveling-diagram.png" alt="Trigonometric leveling geometry showing total station, target, slope distance, zenith angle and elevation difference">
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

